{"code":200,"message":"OK","tweet":{"url":"https://x.com/BrianCChao/status/2036830205629870407","id":"2036830205629870407","text":"This project started with a simple question: why are we still running full attention calculations for background pixels we aren’t even looking at? In many applications, such as interactive gaming and robotics simulation, only selective regions require high-resolution generation.\n\nOur new work, Foveated Diffusion, brings the biological efficiency of the human visual system to Diffusion Transformers by directly reducing the token count through a perceptually-motivated design, adding a new axis to the scaling laws of generative AI.\n\nSee the full breakdown in @GordonWetzstein's post below:","raw_text":{"text":"This project started with a simple question: why are we still running full attention calculations for background pixels we aren’t even looking at? In many applications, such as interactive gaming and robotics simulation, only selective regions require high-resolution generation.\n\nOur new work, Foveated Diffusion, brings the biological efficiency of the human visual system to Diffusion Transformers by directly reducing the token count through a perceptually-motivated design, adding a new axis to the scaling laws of generative AI.\n\nSee the full breakdown in @GordonWetzstein's post below:","display_text_range":[0,592],"facets":[{"type":"bold","indices":[295,313]},{"type":"mention","indices":[562,578],"original":"GordonWetzstein","id":"107572196"}]},"author":{"screen_name":"BrianCChao","url":"https://x.com/BrianCChao","id":"1426168059832635393","followers":700,"following":475,"likes":695,"media_count":30,"name":"Brian Chao","description":"Ph.D. student @Stanford · @NSF Graduate Fellow","raw_description":{"text":"Ph.D. student @Stanford · @NSF Graduate Fellow","facets":[]},"location":"","banner_url":"","avatar_url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2009449635450863617/8b3Y1zMZ_200x200.jpg","joined":"Fri Aug 13 13:05:51 +0000 2021","protected":false,"website":{"url":"https://bchao1.github.io","display_url":"bchao1.github.io"},"verification":{"verified":true,"verified_at":null,"type":"individual"},"avatar_color":null},"replies":6,"retweets":10,"likes":130,"bookmarks":53,"quotes":4,"created_at":"Wed Mar 25 15:38:58 +0000 2026","created_timestamp":1774453138,"views":24064,"is_note_tweet":true,"community_note":null,"lang":"en","replying_to":null,"replying_to_status":null,"quote":{"url":"https://x.com/GordonWetzstein/status/2036819672507793643","id":"2036819672507793643","text":"High-resolution image and video generation is hitting a wall because attention in DiTs scales quadratically with token count. But does every pixel need to be in full resolution?\n\nIntroducing Foveated Diffusion: a new approach for efficient diffusion-based generation that allocates compute where it matters most.\n\n1/7🧵","raw_text":{"text":"High-resolution image and video generation is hitting a wall because attention in DiTs scales quadratically with token count. But does every pixel need to be in full resolution?\n\nIntroducing Foveated Diffusion: a new approach for efficient diffusion-based generation that allocates compute where it matters most.\n\n1/7🧵","display_text_range":[0,319],"facets":[{"type":"media","indices":[272,295],"id":"2036810945264287744","display":"pic.x.com/Gy0QPK4jrX","original":"https://t.co/Gy0QPK4jrX","replacement":"https://x.com/GordonWetzstein/status/2036819672507793643/video/1"}]},"author":{"screen_name":"GordonWetzstein","url":"https://x.com/GordonWetzstein","id":"107572196","followers":5450,"following":51,"likes":164,"media_count":100,"name":"Gordon Wetzstein","description":"Professor at Stanford University & Co-founder at Rhoda AI","raw_description":{"text":"Professor at Stanford University & Co-founder at Rhoda AI","facets":[]},"location":"","banner_url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/107572196/1773120012","avatar_url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/527589449333350400/9X4r